Body:
## Proposed fix + validation results

Following up on the root-cause comment: we validated fix candidates against `@opentui/core` 0.4.5 with a painted-frame harness (`captureCharFrame()` after `pasteBracketedText`, rather than reading the buffer — buffer reads always pass and mask this bug).

### Results (0.4.5, bun harness)

| Variant | Buffer | Painted frame |
|---|---|---|
| A) bare `<textarea>` (current dialog code) | ✓ | ✓ |
| B) `<textarea onContentChange={() => renderer.requestRender()} />` | ✓ | ✓ |
| C) composer-style `onPaste` self-insert | ✓ | ✓ |

Notable: **on 0.4.5 even variant A paints** — meaning the missing-repaint behavior regressed somewhere between the published 0.4.5 and whatever @opentui/core build is bundled into the running binary (0.0.0-beta-18138; its bundle is minified so we couldn't diff statically — worth auditing what opentui revision the release embeds vs. the `catalog:` pin).

### Recommended fix (works regardless of the embedded opentui revision)

In `packages/tui/src/routes/session/question.tsx`, give the custom-answer textarea the same reactive wiring the composer relies on — the renderer reference is already in scope:

```tsx
<textarea
  ref={(val: TextareaRenderable) => {
    textarea = val
    val.traits = { status: "ANSWER" }
    queueMicrotask(() => { val.focus(); val.gotoLineEnd() })
  }}
  initialValue={input()}
  placeholder="Type your own answer"
  placeholderColor={theme.textMuted}
  minHeight={1}
  maxHeight={6}
  textColor={theme.text}
  focusedTextColor={theme.text}
  cursorColor={theme.primary}
  cursorStyle={tuiConfig.cursor}
  onContentChange={() => renderer.requestRender()}
/>
```

This guarantees a frame on every buffer mutation (paste included) even if the embedded core stops self-scheduling renders on programmatic inserts. Optionally also file upstream on @opentui/core: `EditBufferRenderable.insertText()` triggered via a paste event should mark the renderable dirty / wake the render loop when idle.

Happy to test a patched build — the reporter can reproduce on demand within seconds using their dictation setup.
